Blocked-by: #1517
Not-before: 2026-09-01T09:00:00Z
Retry-every: 1 day
Model: opus

The last step of #1492 / #1494. The reader has been on every member since `claudinite-tasks` 60831.3; the line is on none of them. #1511 re-opened the lane that can carry it. This is the record that uses it.

## Why it was not shipped with #1511

A record is selected only while `recordVersion > installedVersion` (`packRecordsInGap` → `migrationApplies`), and **the executing worker is the member's own vendored copy** — the vendor step replaces `pack-update.mjs` on disk while the old code is still running. So a record shipped beside #1511 would have run against the OLD dropping `write`, no-opped, been stamped past, and never been selected again. `minEngineVersion` gates on the engine and cannot express "needs `claudinite-lifecycle` >= X".

So the precondition is a converge-cycle-confirmable fact, not a date: **every member stamps `claudinite-lifecycle` >= 60831.1.** #1517 is what establishes it.

## The record, written and validated

Lives at `packs/claudinite-tasks/migrations/2026-08-31-executor-vars-bag/migration.mjs`, with `version` set to the `claudinite-tasks` version this change bumps to (it was `60831.6` when drafted; re-derive it, the pack has moved).

```js
const EXECUTOR = '.github/workflows/claudinite-executor.yml';
const HOLD = '          CLAUDINITE_TASKS_SUSPEND_ALL: ${{ vars.CLAUDINITE_TASKS_SUSPEND_ALL }}\n';
// BAG = the six comment lines + `CLAUDINITE_VARS: ${{ toJSON(vars) }}`, at 10-space indent,
// identical to what packs/claudinite-tasks/stubs/claudinite-executor.yml carries.

export default {
  id: 'executor-vars-bag',
  landed: '2026-08-31',
  version: '<the claudinite-tasks version this ships at>',
  summary: 'the live executor workflow carries CLAUDINITE_VARS (#1492, #1494)',
  appliesTo: async (read) => {
    const text = await read(EXECUTOR);
    if (!text) return false;
    return text.includes(HOLD) && !text.includes('CLAUDINITE_VARS:');
  },
  rewrite: [{ file: EXECUTOR, replace: [{ from: HOLD, to: HOLD + BAG }] }],
  legacyPresent: async (_exists, read) => {
    const text = await read(EXECUTOR);
    return Boolean(text) && text.includes(HOLD) && !text.includes('CLAUDINITE_VARS:');
  },
};
```

Three decisions in it that are not obvious and should survive review:

- **A `rewrite`, not a `materialize`.** The executor is not identical across members — the wiring converge stamps each one's own `required_secrets` beneath the `# claudinite:secrets` marker. Copying the stub over it would deliver the line and take every member's secrets with it.
- **Idempotency lives in `appliesTo`.** `applyRewrites` uses split/join, so a second run against an already-rewritten file would insert a *second* copy of the block. The `!text.includes('CLAUDINITE_VARS:')` clause is what makes that impossible; the version gate alone is not enough.
- **The anchor is the operator hold, not the `# claudinite:secrets` marker.** Anchoring to the marker would put the bag inside the region the wiring converge regenerates, where the next converge would overwrite it.

Its test (`executor-vars-bag: inserts the bag, preserves each member's stamped secrets, and re-runs as a no-op`) was written and passing before being pulled out — it asserts the member's own secret survives, the marker survives, the bag lands *above* the marker, and a second `appliesTo` returns false.

## What the run does

1. Confirm the precondition: every member stamps `claudinite-lifecycle` >= 60831.1. Not yet → push `Not-before:` forward by `Retry-every:` and leave it open.
2. Re-create the record and its test, bump `claudinite-tasks`, land it.
3. Force fleet delivery and report per member — the line reaching a member's live `.github/workflows/claudinite-executor.yml` is the only artifact that counts, not a run conclusion.
4. That delivery is also what finally exercises the apply stage end to end, which #1511 shipped and nothing has yet driven.

Refs #1492, #1494, #1509, #1511

